{"id":"q1-02-r2","title":"Normalization (1NF to BCNF) and when to denormalize","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: update/insert/delete anomalies, functional dependencies, 1NF to BCNF, and safe denormalization techniques. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"why-normalization-exists-anomalies","title":"Why normalization exists: anomalies","html":"<p><strong>Normalization is organising tables so each fact is stored exactly once.</strong> If a fact lives in many places, they drift apart, and you get three classic bugs called anomalies.</p>\n<p>Imagine one big table <code>orders_flat(order_id, customer_name, customer_city, product, price)</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Update anomaly:</strong> a customer moves city; you must update 400 rows; miss one and the data contradicts itself.</li>\n<li><strong>Insert anomaly:</strong> you can't record a new customer until they place an order.</li>\n<li><strong>Delete anomaly:</strong> deleting the customer's only order also erases the fact that the customer exists.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 490 192\" width=\"490\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One fat table versus split tables\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M158.4 96 L214.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M158.4 96 L214.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M332 96 L388 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M332 96 L388 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M332 96 L388 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M332 96 L388 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M332 96 L388 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M332 96 L388 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"85.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Orders flat table</text><rect x=\"214.4\" y=\"74\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"273.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Split by fact</text><rect x=\"388\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"433\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Customers</text><rect x=\"388\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"433\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Orders</text><rect x=\"388\" y=\"136\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"433\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Products</text></svg><figcaption>One fat table versus split tables</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 1M orders from 50k customers. In the flat table the city string repeats 20 times per customer on average: 1M x ~12 bytes = 12 MB of redundant city text, and one move means touching ~20 rows. Normalised: 50k city values, one row update.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Core OLTP systems (banking ledgers, Stripe's customer/charge tables, Shopify orders) are normalised because correctness beats a few extra joins. Analytics warehouses (BigQuery, Redshift) deliberately denormalise, which is the next-to-last section.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Writing your phone number on 30 sticky notes. When it changes, you will forget one note.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Defining normalization as \"splitting tables\". The goal is one fact in one place.</li>\n<li>Not being able to name the three anomalies with an example.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"functional-dependencies-the-tool-behind-everything","title":"Functional dependencies (the tool behind everything)","html":"<p><strong>A functional dependency <code>A -> B</code> means: if two rows have the same A, they must have the same B.</strong> <code>customer_id -> customer_city</code> holds because a customer lives in one city. <code>order_id, product_id -> qty</code> holds in an order-lines table.</p>\n<p>A <strong>candidate key</strong> is a minimal set of columns that determines every other column. Normal forms are rules about which dependencies are allowed relative to the keys.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>orders_flat(order_id, product_id, customer_id, customer_city, product_name, qty)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Key: (order_id, product_id)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  order_id               -> customer_id          (part of key only: partial dependency)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  customer_id            -> customer_city        (non-key determines non-key: transitive)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  product_id             -> product_name         (part of key only)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  order_id, product_id   -> qty                  (full key: fine)</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Vocabulary: <strong>prime attribute</strong> = part of some candidate key. <strong>Non-prime</strong> = not part of any key. <strong>Partial dependency</strong> = non-prime depends on part of a composite key. <strong>Transitive dependency</strong> = key -> X -> Y where X is not a key.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 482.79999999999995 68\" width=\"482.79999999999995\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Reading a dependency\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 34 L317.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 34 L317.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Key columns</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Determine</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Every other column</text></svg><figcaption>Reading a dependency</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> In the table above, <code>order_id -> customer_id</code> means every order line repeats the customer. If an order has 10 lines, <code>customer_id</code> is stored 10 times; changing the customer on an order means 10 writes and a chance of 9.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A postcode determines the city. If your address book stores both, the city is redundant given the postcode.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mixing up the direction: <code>A -> B</code> does not imply <code>B -> A</code>.</li>\n<li>Forgetting to first identify the key before judging a normal form.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"1nf-atomic-values-no-repeating-groups","title":"1NF: atomic values, no repeating groups","html":"<p><strong>First normal form: every column holds a single indivisible value, every row is unique, and there are no repeating column groups.</strong></p>\n<p>Violations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A column storing <code>'red,green,blue'</code> or a JSON array you query inside.</li>\n<li>Repeating columns: <code>phone1, phone2, phone3</code>.</li>\n<li>No key at all, so duplicate rows can exist.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- Bad: list in a column</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> TABLE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> student_bad</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (id </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> PRIMARY KEY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">name</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> text</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, courses </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">text</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">); </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- 'math,physics'</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- 1NF: one row per fact</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> TABLE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> enrolment</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  student_id </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, course </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">text</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">  PRIMARY KEY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (student_id, course)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- Now this is a plain index lookup instead of LIKE '%physics%' (full scan)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">SELECT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> student_id </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">FROM</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> enrolment </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">WHERE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> course </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> 'physics'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 554.8 130\" width=\"554.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Fixing a repeating group\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M208.8 65 L264.8 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M208.8 65 L264.8 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M354.8 65 L410.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M354.8 65 L410.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M354.8 65 L410.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M354.8 65 L410.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"196.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"110.4\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Student with list column</text><rect x=\"264.8\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"309.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Split</text><rect x=\"410.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"476.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Student table</text><rect x=\"410.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"476.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Enrolment table</text></svg><figcaption>Fixing a repeating group</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Finding students of <code>physics</code> with <code>LIKE '%physics%'</code> over 2M rows needs a seq scan, about 100 to 400 ms. After 1NF with an index on <code>course</code>, it is under 1 ms plus the rows returned. Also <code>'physics'</code> vs <code>'astrophysics'</code> stops matching by accident.</p>\n<p><strong>Grey zone.</strong> Postgres arrays and <code>jsonb</code> technically break the strict rule, yet are fine when you treat the value as opaque or index it with GIN and never need joins or per-element constraints. Be able to say that nuance.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Early MySQL apps with CSV-in-a-column tags were a common migration pain; tag systems (GitHub labels, Stack Overflow tags) use a junction table.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> One item per line on a shopping list rather than \"milk, eggs, bread\" all on one line, so you can tick items off one at a time.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying arrays/jsonb always violate 1NF. It is about how you use them.</li>\n<li>Forgetting that a table with no PK can hold duplicates.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"2nf-no-partial-dependencies","title":"2NF: no partial dependencies","html":"<p><strong>Second normal form: be in 1NF, and every non-key column depends on the WHOLE key, not just part of it.</strong> This only matters when the key is composite.</p>\n<p>Table <code>order_line(order_id, product_id, qty, product_name)</code> with key <code>(order_id, product_id)</code>. <code>product_name</code> depends on <code>product_id</code> alone: partial dependency.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- Split product facts out</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> TABLE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> product</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (product_id </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> PRIMARY KEY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, product_name </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">text</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> NOT NULL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> TABLE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> order_line</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  order_id </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, product_id </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> REFERENCES</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> product,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  qty </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> NOT NULL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">  PRIMARY KEY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (order_id, product_id)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 698.8000000000001 130\" width=\"698.8000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"2NF split\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M237.6 65 L293.6 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M237.6 65 L293.6 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M383.6 65 L439.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M383.6 65 L439.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M383.6 65 L439.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M383.6 65 L439.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"225.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"124.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">order_line with product_name</text><rect x=\"293.6\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"338.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Split</text><rect x=\"439.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"247.20000000000002\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"563.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">product</text><rect x=\"439.6\" y=\"74\" width=\"247.20000000000002\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"563.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">order_line without product_name</text></svg><figcaption>2NF split</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 20M order lines, <code>product_name</code> averaging 30 bytes: 600 MB of repeated names. After 2NF, 100k products x 30 B = 3 MB, and renaming a product is one row.</p>\n<p><strong>Careful.</strong> Snapshot columns (price at the time of sale) look like partial dependencies but are deliberate: the price at purchase time is a fact about the order line, not about the product today.</p>\n<p><strong>If the key is a single column</strong>, a table in 1NF is automatically in 2NF.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Every order system keeps a <code>product</code> table and references it; Shopify copies title and price into <code>line_items</code> as a snapshot on purpose.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A receipt shows quantity per product; it should not retell each product's whole description every line.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Claiming snapshot columns violate 2NF. They record a historical fact.</li>\n<li>Applying 2NF to single-column-key tables (always satisfied).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"3nf-no-transitive-dependencies","title":"3NF: no transitive dependencies","html":"<p><strong>Third normal form: be in 2NF, and no non-key column depends on another non-key column.</strong> \"Every non-key column depends on the key, the whole key, and nothing but the key.\"</p>\n<p><code>employee(emp_id PK, dept_id, dept_name)</code>: <code>emp_id -> dept_id -> dept_name</code>. <code>dept_name</code> depends on <code>dept_id</code>, not directly on the key.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> TABLE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> department</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (dept_id </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> PRIMARY KEY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, dept_name </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">text</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> NOT NULL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> TABLE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> employee</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  emp_id  </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> PRIMARY KEY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  dept_id </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> NOT NULL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> REFERENCES</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> department</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 406 68\" width=\"406\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Remove the middle step\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">employee</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">dept_id</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">dept_name</text></svg><figcaption>Remove the middle step</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Renaming \"Engineering\" to \"Platform\" in the flat table touches all 8,000 engineers (and risks inconsistency, \"Engineering\" and \"Platform\" both existing). In 3NF it is one row update.</p>\n<p><strong>Formal 3NF (for interviews).</strong> For each dependency <code>X -> A</code>, either X is a superkey, or A is part of some candidate key. The second clause is what BCNF removes.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Most ORM-modelled business apps are 3NF by default. Reference data (countries, currencies, statuses) lives in lookup tables.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Normalising is reversible (you can denormalise later with a view or copy), and splitting a table in production is a migration, not a catastrophe. Over-normalising a hot read path is the more common regret, handled in the last section.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A student card shows the school ID, not the school's full address; the address lives in one school record.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying 3NF means \"no redundancy at all\". Some remains (keys repeat as FKs).</li>\n<li>Not knowing the \"key, whole key, nothing but the key\" summary.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"bcnf-every-determinant-is-a-key","title":"BCNF: every determinant is a key","html":"<p><strong>Boyce-Codd normal form: for every dependency <code>X -> Y</code>, X must be a superkey.</strong> It is a stricter 3NF that closes a loophole when a table has overlapping candidate keys.</p>\n<p>Example: <code>class_slot(student, subject, teacher)</code>. Rules: each teacher teaches ONE subject; a student has one teacher per subject. Keys: <code>(student, subject)</code> and <code>(student, teacher)</code>. Dependency <code>teacher -> subject</code> exists, but <code>teacher</code> is not a key. This is in 3NF (subject is part of a key) but violates BCNF: teacher \"Rao -> Maths\" is repeated for every student.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> TABLE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> teacher_subject</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (teacher </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">text</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> PRIMARY KEY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">subject</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> text</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> NOT NULL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> TABLE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> student_teacher</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  student </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">text</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, teacher </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">text</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> REFERENCES</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> teacher_subject,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">  PRIMARY KEY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (student, teacher)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 503.2 130\" width=\"503.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"BCNF decomposition\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 65 L164 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 65 L164 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M303.2 65 L359.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M303.2 65 L359.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M303.2 65 L359.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M303.2 65 L359.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">class_slot</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"43\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"233.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Split on teacher</text><rect x=\"359.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"425.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">teacher_subject</text><rect x=\"359.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"425.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">student_teacher</text></svg><figcaption>BCNF decomposition</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Trade-off.</strong> BCNF decomposition may lose the ability to enforce the rule \"a student has one teacher per subject\" with a plain key constraint (you can't express <code>(student, subject)</code> uniqueness across the split without a trigger or extra join). That is why some designs stay at 3NF. 3NF is always lossless and dependency preserving; BCNF is lossless but not always dependency preserving.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 100k students x 6 subjects = 600k rows. Before: Rao's subject repeated 600k/200 teachers = 3,000 times each. After: 200 rows in <code>teacher_subject</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Higher forms, one line each.</strong> 4NF removes independent multi-valued facts stored together (a person's hobbies and languages in one table, causing a cross product). 5NF removes join dependencies. 6NF is temporal (one fact per row over time). Interviews rarely go past BCNF/4NF.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A timetable listing \"teacher Rao, subject Maths\" on every student line, instead of one board saying Rao teaches Maths.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Believing 3NF and BCNF are the same. They differ with overlapping candidate keys.</li>\n<li>Saying BCNF is always better; dependency preservation can be lost.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"when-to-denormalize","title":"When to denormalize","html":"<p><strong>Denormalization is deliberately storing the same fact in more than one place to make reads cheaper.</strong> You pay with write complexity and risk of drift. Normalise first; denormalise with a measurement in hand.</p>\n<p>Common techniques:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Copy a column</strong> (store <code>author_name</code> in <code>posts</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Precomputed counters</strong> (<code>comment_count</code> on <code>posts</code>) so you avoid <code>COUNT(*)</code> over millions of rows.</li>\n<li><strong>Summary / rollup tables</strong> (daily revenue per shop) refreshed by jobs.</li>\n<li><strong>Materialized views</strong> (Postgres <code>CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW</code>, refresh manually or on schedule).</li>\n<li><strong>jsonb snapshot</strong> of a related object.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> MATERIALIZED VIEW daily_revenue </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">AS</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">  SELECT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> date_trunc(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">'day'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, created_at) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">AS</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> d, shop_id, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">sum</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(total_cents) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">AS</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> cents</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">  FROM</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> orders </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">GROUP BY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">2</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> UNIQUE INDEX</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> ON</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> daily_revenue (d, shop_id);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY daily_revenue;  </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- needs the unique index</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 582.4 130\" width=\"582.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Keeping a counter in sync\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M136.8 65 L192.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M136.8 65 L192.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M332 34 L388 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M332 34 L388 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M136.8 65 L192.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M136.8 65 L192.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"74.4\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Insert comment</text><rect x=\"192.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"262.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Same transaction</text><rect x=\"192.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"262.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">comments table</text><rect x=\"388\" y=\"43\" width=\"182.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"479.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Increment post counter</text></svg><figcaption>Keeping a counter in sync</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Feed page needs author name for 20 posts. Join cost: 20 index lookups, about 1 ms total, so DON'T denormalise this. But <code>SELECT count(*) FROM likes WHERE post_id = X</code> on a 10-billion-row table with a celebrity post of 50M likes costs seconds; a stored <code>like_count</code> makes it O(1), updated by a queue or sharded counters (hot row contention becomes the new problem: 50k increments/s on one row serialises on its lock).</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Instagram and Twitter store like/follower counts as counters, accepting slight lag. Data warehouses use star schemas (fact table plus denormalised dimensions) to cut joins for analytics. Stack Overflow keeps <code>Score</code>/<code>AnswerCount</code> columns on <code>Posts</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Adding a derived column is easy and reversible; keeping it correct for years is the real cost. Prefer: constraint or trigger or one write path; add a periodic reconcile job that recomputes and alerts on drift.</p>\n<p><strong>Production incident pattern.</strong> Counter drifts after a retry double-counts. Symptom: user sees \"3 comments\" but lists 2. Metric: reconcile job's mismatch count rises. Fix: make updates idempotent (derive from events) or recompute.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Keeping a running total on the cashier's screen instead of re-adding the whole receipt each time. Fast, but if you forget to update it, it lies.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Denormalising on day one without measuring; first fix indexes and queries.</li>\n<li>Not saying how you keep the copy consistent.</li>\n<li>Ignoring hot-row contention on a shared counter.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Normalization = one fact in one place; it prevents update, insert and delete anomalies.</li>\n<li>Functional dependency <code>A -> B</code> is the tool; find the key first.</li>\n<li>1NF atomic values; 2NF no partial dependency on a composite key; 3NF no transitive dependency (\"key, whole key, nothing but the key\"); BCNF every determinant is a superkey.</li>\n<li>3NF is always lossless and dependency preserving; BCNF may lose dependency preservation.</li>\n<li>Snapshots (price at sale) are deliberate, not violations.</li>\n<li>Denormalise only with measurements: counters, rollups, materialized views, copied columns; plan a reconcile job.</li>\n<li>Normalise first (reversible, cheap); denormalising a hot path later is safer than guessing early.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}